  "explanation": "The question asks 'When was the South Calgary electoral district created?' and must be interpreted with care due to overlapping uses of the name 'South Calgary' in different contexts (provincial vs. federal, first creation vs. re-creation). The relevant sources clarify:\n\n- **Document D2S4** states: 'The South Calgary electoral district was created in 1913 when the Calgary provincial electoral district was carved into three ridings.' This refers to the **first provincial creation**.\n- **Document D1S6** states: 'The first provincial electoral district to use the name Calgary South East was created in the 1959 redistribution...' This refers to a **different configuration** under the same general name.\n- **Document D1S2** states: 'It has existed twice, first from 1959 to 1963, and then re-created in 2010.' This confirms a **second creation in 2010**.\n\nThe year **1986** (from Document D3S4) refers to the **federal electoral district**, which is a separate entity and not relevant to the question about the **provincial** South Calgary electoral district. Therefore, it is removed."
}
